Now add blob shadow to car model. Best place: create a circular gradient texture? We can make a mesh with a radial alpha texture generated via canvas, mesh basic material transparent, depthWrite false, rotation -PI/2, positioned at ground y + 0.03, follows car root. Since the car root position.y is surface + 0.02; shadow at local y ~0.035. But body may pitch; shadow attached to root, not body. Add to root in carModel. Size: length*1.0, width*1.2. Use canvas radial gradient black transparent. This grounds all cars (menu, garage? garage preview maybe no floor shadow). For player car good. The garage has its own floor/lighting.

Also perhaps low quality should still cast simple shadows? No, blob shadow is efficient.

Let's implement in carModel.js after root creation. Need generate texture once (module-level cache) and material per car. Use THREE.CanvasTexture. Some sizes.

```
let shadowTex;
function getShadowTexture() {
  if (shadowTex) return shadowTex;
  const c = document.createElement('canvas'); c.width = c.height = 128;
  const ctx = c.getContext('2d');
  const g = ctx.createRadialGradient(64,64,8,64,64,64);
  g.addColorStop(0,'rgba(0,0,0,0.55)'); g.addColorStop(0.55,'rgba(0,0,0,0.28)'); g.addColorStop(1,'rgba(0,0,0,0)');
  ctx.fillStyle = g; ctx.fillRect(0,0,128,128);
  shadowTex = new THREE.CanvasTexture(c); shadowTex.colorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace? Actually for alpha, linear. colorSpace = SRGBColorSpace? Basic black no difference. 
  return shadowTex;
}
```

Then:
```
const shadow = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(Wd*1.35, L*1.15), new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({map:getShadowTexture(), transparent:true, depthWrite:false, opacity:0.85, toneMapped:false}));
shadow.rotation.x = -Math.PI/2;
shadow.position.y = 0.04;
shadow.renderOrder = 2;
root.add(shadow);
```
But plane geometry 1.35*width, length. Position at root local y=0.04; root at surface+0.02 so 0.06 above ground; z-fighting unlikely. Needs to orient with car; plane in XZ. Put on root before body. It will tilt with root? Root rotates y only. Fine. It may be clipped on slopes, but okay.

Set material polygonOffset to avoid z-fighting, and depthTest true. Since ground may be at varying height, shadow floats. Still acceptable. Maybe use `polygonOffset: true, polygonOffsetFactor: -4`.

Need ensure `dispose` disposes shadow geometry/material? texture shared. Material per model. Check model.dispose function.

